# DSGW-210: replaces systemd's 90-vconsole.rules with an empty rule set.
#
# Upstream rule: on every vtconsole "add" uevent udev runs
#   /usr/bin/systemctl --no-block restart systemd-vconsole-setup.service
# The DSGW-210 is headless (no VOP/HDMI in its DT), so there is no console
# to set up; the unit is masked next to this file (etc/systemd/system/).
#
# This file deliberately overrides the copy in /usr/lib rather than masking
# it from /etc/udev/rules.d: on HAOS /etc/udev/rules.d is bind-mounted from
# the overlay partition (etc-udev-rules.d.mount) and is wiped by haos-config
# when CONFIG/udev exists, so an /etc override in the rootfs would vanish
# from udev's view after that mount.
